 ### 6.6 Gohan's outfit (owner)
 
 After his Hyperbolic Time Chamber training, Gohan wears the purple Piccolo-style gi in every form once he is playable again (owner).
 
 - In LoG II the player loses Gohan before the training (in the Demon Clothes) and gets him back after it in armor.
 - The cutscenes between the training and the point where Gohan is playable keep the armor. From the moment he is playable, he wears the gi.
 - A later slice may add a short scene where Gohan changes into the gi. Not in slice 1.
 - Owner, 2026-10-16: once Gohan has the gi (from the first moment he is playable after the chamber), every later cutscene and NPC appearance uses the gi too. This includes the Cell Games Arena NPC and the post-Cell scene (`docs\re-outfit.md` section 5). Slice 1 leaves these in armor on purpose; change them in the slice after the owner tests slice 1.
 
+- Hair (owner, 2026-10-16): base-form Gohan keeps the shorter hair of the armor sprites (set 56), not the longer Android saga hair of the Demon Clothes set 53. Head and hair come from set 56, the body from set 53.
+- Chest (owner, 2026-10-16): all three gi forms open the collar into a small V-neck, like Piccolo. A hint only, never a bare chest: the gi covers the torso. Front frames: a narrow V at most 2 pixels deep. Side frames: at most 1 skin pixel at the collar, or none. Back frames: no torso skin. Existing skin palette indices only.
 - Base: the LoG II Demon Clothes frames (sprite set 53), edited:
   - Remove the white neck piece.
   - Boots match Piccolo's sprite (brown, palette 34 and 35).
   - The purple moves toward Piccolo's gi (palette 88 and 89).
   - Red sash. Blue wristbands.
 - References: `data\reference\D6FHgvhUIAATrwf.jpg` (manga, Cell Games), `images.jpg`, the Piccolo sprite.
 - Portraits: the International portrait sheet appears to show Super Saiyan Gohan in the gi. Port those portraits for every form.
 
 ### 6.7 Backlog candidates (not agreed)
 
 - Owner idea (2026-10-16), after slice 1 proves the art pipeline: bring the Buu's Fury Piccolo and Goku sprites into LoG II. Sheets are in `data\sprites\`.
+  - Piccolo risk (owner): in LoG II, Piccolo's transform removes his turban and cape. Buu's Fury has no such frames, and its cape is larger. The transform and the caped and uncaped frame sets must be planned.
+  - Owner scope (2026-10-16): no patch to Buu's Fury and no Buu's Fury code work. Read-only asset extraction is allowed (Ruling 34).
+- Owner idea (2026-10-16): look at the Buu's Fury stat screen look for LoG II.
