+# LOG reverse engineering bible
+
+The single index of everything known about the ROMs. Every fact is one line with search tags. Detail and evidence live in the linked source document.
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> **Rule:** every session and every task that learns a fact adds one line here in the same session, with its label and its source. A fact that is not in this file is treated as unknown.
+
+---
+
+## 1. How to search
+
+Use these tag shapes. Each one is unique, so a plain text search finds every line about it.
+
+| Search for | Finds |
+|---|---|
+| `@0x0801F394` | A GBA address (code, ROM data as `@0x08xxxxxx`, RAM as `@0x02xxxxxx` or `@0x03xxxxxx`) |
+| `rom:0x3B4E90` | A file offset in the ROM (address minus `0x08000000`) |
+| `flag:195` | A story flag |
+| `set:56` | A sprite set id |
+| `pal:88` | A shared OBJ palette index |
+| `char:gohan` | A character (`gohan`, `piccolo`, `vegeta`, `trunks`, `goku`, `hercule`) |
+| `#codec` `#sprite` `#save` `#form` `#story` `#map` `#palette` `#hud` `#portrait` `#text` `#script` `#antipiracy` `#debug` `#tool` `#decision` `#open` | A topic |
+| `game:bf` `game:log2eu` | A fact about Buu's Fury or the Europe LoG II. No game tag means LoG II USA |
+
+Labels: **C** = CONFIRMED (proved, evidence in the source doc), **L** = LIKELY, **S** = SPECULATIVE, **O** = owner statement (from memory or play, not checked in the ROM).
+
+Source docs: `RN` = `research-notes.md`, `SPR` = `re-sprite-decompression.md`, `SAV` = `re-save-format.md`, `DES` = `2026-10-16-log-merge-design.md`, `OUT` = `re-outfit.md`, `FRM` = `re-forms.md`, `T5` = `scratch\sdd\slice1\task-5-report.md`, `T5P2` = `scratch\sdd\slice1\task-5-part2-report.md`. Add new docs to this list.
+
